```mdl
test T-Run-Edge-Kinds-Accepted: createEdge accepts 'is-run-of' and 'parent-run'    # Iteration 2b
  given: a Bramble graph; the Run + Step supertag classes are registered
  when: code calls `createEdge(db, stepNode, runNode, { kind: 'is-run-of' })` and `createEdge(db, parentRun, childRun, { kind: 'parent-run' })`
  then:
    - both edges persist with the requested `kind`
    - neither edge appears in `childEdgesOf(parentNode)` (kind filter still 'child'-only)
    - cycle detection is skipped for non-'child' kinds (verified by creating a cycle that would be rejected if `kind: 'child'`)
```

```mdl
test T-New-Run-On-Step: "+ New Run" creates a Run-tree + zooms into the parent    # Iteration 2c.1 (revised)
  given: a Bramble graph with a Node S tagged `#Step` carrying N >= 0 `#Step`-tagged structural descendants (sub-Steps, sub-sub-Steps, …); the user is viewing S as the page node
  when: user clicks the "+ New Run" button
  then:
    - exactly 1 + N new Bramble.Nodes are added, all tagged `#Run`
    - the parent Run-Node has an Edge `kind: 'is-run-of'` → S
    - for every `#Step`-tagged descendant D of S, exactly one child Run-Node exists with `kind: 'is-run-of'` → D and `kind: 'parent-run'` → the Run-Node of D's parent Step
    - the current pane's page-node is the parent Run-Node
    - F-Run-Execution-View renders (NOT the Graph outline); the runbook prompt for S is visible at the top
    - "+ New Run" does NOT appear on the new Run-Node's page (gated on `#Step`)
```

```mdl
test T-Run-Lens-Lifecycle: full Start → Next → Done lifecycle    # Iteration 2c.5
  given: a Bramble graph with a Step S and `#Step`-tagged sub-Steps S1 / S2 / S3
  when: user clicks "+ New Run" on S's page
  then:
    - a parent Run-Node and three child Run-Nodes are spawned (per F-New-Run-On-Step)
    - the pane zooms into the parent Run-Node
    - Article's `runLensActive` is true (Lens activates automatically)
    - RunLensShell renders with sky-tinted banner + "Start / Stop / Done" controls visible
    - "Done" is disabled (no responses filled in yet)
  when: user clicks "Start"
  then:
    - "Start" button disappears; "Previous / Next" buttons appear
    - the active Run-Node is the parent Run-Node (depth-first first), highlighted with a sky ring
    - "Previous" is disabled (at index 0)
  when: user clicks "Next" three times
  then:
    - the active Run-Node advances through S1, S2, S3
    - the sky ring follows the active Run-Node
    - at index 3 (the last), "Next" is disabled
  when: user types responses into each Run-Node's outline body (adds bullets with text)
  then:
    - "Done" becomes enabled reactively as the database changes
  when: user clicks "Done"
  then:
    - the Run supertag instance gains a `completed` field with an ISO-8601 timestamp
    - `runLensActive` becomes false
    - a "Resume in Run Lens" button replaces the wizard banner
    - the RunExecutionView still renders below in plain (non-Lens) mode
  when: user clicks "Stop" instead of Done at any point
  then: same as Done EXCEPT the `completed` field is NOT set
```

```mdl
test T-Step-Runs-List: `#Step` page lists every Run linked to it    # Iteration 2d
  given: a Bramble graph with a Node S tagged `#Step` and three top-level Run-Nodes R1 / R2 / R3, each with an `'is-run-of'` edge → S
  when: the user opens S as the page node
  then:
    - between the "+ New Run" button and the outline body, a "Runs (3)" list appears
    - the list has three rows in chronological order (oldest first; R1 before R2 before R3)
    - clicking R2's row zooms the pane into R2 (its F-Run-Execution-View renders)
    - shift-clicking R3's row opens R3 in a new pane
  when: the Step has zero Runs
  then:
    - no Runs list panel renders (the "+ New Run" button is the only call-to-action)
```

```mdl
test T-Run-Nav: page-top nav surfaces 'is-run-of' and 'parent-run' edges    # Iteration 2c.2 follow-up
  given: a top-level Run-Node R linked via `'is-run-of'` to Step S, with at least one child Run R' linked via `'parent-run'` → R
  when: the user opens R as the page node
  then:
    - a nav link "← Step: {S.label}" appears above the runbook view
    - no "↑ Parent run" link appears (R is top-level, has no `'parent-run'` edge)
    - clicking the Step link zooms the pane into S
    - shift-clicking the Step link opens S in a new pane
  when: the user opens R' as the page node
  then:
    - both "← Step: {sub-Step label}" AND "↑ Parent run: {R.label or '(untitled run)'}" links appear
    - clicking the parent-run link zooms the pane into R
```

```mdl
test T-Run-Execution-View-Renders: page Node tagged `#Run` shows a structured walkthrough    # Iteration 2c.2
  given: a Run-Node R that is `'is-run-of'` Step S, where S has content "Reconcile EOB" and 2 sub-Steps S1 / S2 (with their own content and their own child Run-Nodes R1 / R2 linked via `'parent-run'` → R)
  when: the user opens R as the page node
  then:
    - the page H1 renders R per existing PageHeader rules
    - the Graph outline view is NOT rendered
    - F-Run-Execution-View renders: S's content as a read-only narrative; an editable bound to R's body; below it, the two child Runs R1 / R2 indented one level, each showing their respective sub-Step's content as read-only narrative and an editable bound to their body
    - typing into R1's editable updates `R1.content` (persistent)
    - typing into R2's editable updates `R2.content`
    - recursion continues: if a sub-Step has its own sub-Step (a #Step-tagged grandchild), the corresponding grandchild Run-Node would render indented one further level
```

```mdl
test T-Supertag-Chips-On-Page-Header: page H1 shows chips for the page Node's supertags    # Iteration 2c.1 follow-up
  given: a Bramble graph with a Node tagged `#Step` (and zoomed into so it is the page node)
