```

```mdl
test T-PDF-Upload-creates-node: dropping a PDF onto a page creates a new bullet whose content is the filename
  given: a Bramble page open on a pane; plugin-wnfs contributes
    `AppCapabilities.FileUploader`; the user has a local PDF
    file F (e.g. ~100 KB) ready to drag from the OS
  when: I drag F onto the article surface and release the
    pointer over an empty area of the page
  then:
    - a new Wnfs.File W is created and added to the space by
      the FileUploader capability;
    - a new Bramble.Node B is created with W as its sole
      supertag (`B.supertags = [Ref(W)]`);
    - B's `content` is a copy of F's name (per
      F-PDF-Upload.drop-seeds-content-with-filename) — the
      bullet displays the filename as editable text;
    - B appears in the page as a fresh bullet under the drop-
      site parent (the page node when the drop did not land
      on a specific bullet), wired in via `createEdge` per
      F-DAG;
    - B's rendered row also shows the #File supertag chip
      followed by a small non-interactive PDF icon per
      F-PDF-Upload.chip-rendering.
```

```mdl
test T-PDF-Upload-dedupes-on-second-drop: dropping the SAME PDF a second time reuses the existing bullet
  given: a PDF is already present in the Bramble — Node X
    wraps the corresponding Wnfs.File (W's `cid` matches the
    bytes), e.g. via T-PDF-Upload-creates-node having just run
  when: I drop the same file onto a Bramble page at a new
    drop site
  then:
    - Node X appears at the new drop site (no new Wnfs.File,
      no new Bramble.Node — the dedup invariants hold);
    - the drop-site parent gains a `'child'`-kind edge
      pointing at X (added via `createEdge` if not already
      present);
    - X is now visible at the new drop point AND at its
      original location; the F-DAG multi-parent badge
      surfaces on every occurrence per F-DAG.Phase3e.
```

```mdl
