```mdl
test T-Mention-Hides-Promotable-Payloads: payload ECHO objects don't appear in the @-mention picker; the wrapping Bramble.Node does
  given: a Composer space with a Bramble outline open in editable
    position
  and: a payload ECHO instance `X` of an external typename `T`
    (e.g. a `Wnfs.File` uploaded via plugin-wnfs's drop affordance,
    a `Task` created by plugin-tasks, or any object created
    outside Bramble) with a non-empty display label `L`
  and: a wrapping Bramble.Node `W` that carries `X` in its
    `supertags` array (per F-Supertag / F-PDF-Upload's wrap
    pattern)
  when: I type `@` in any bullet and then type a substring of
    `L`
  then:
    - the picker lists `W` — a single Bramble.Node entry whose
      resolved display label matches `L` (or matches the renamed
      wrapper label, if the user has renamed the wrapper);
    - the payload `X` is NOT listed (the picker surfaces
      Bramble.Nodes only per R-Bramble-Surfaces-Wrap-Only);
    - no duplicate "`L`" entries appear from a schema-registry-
      enumerated typename filter path.
  given: a payload ECHO instance `Y` of an external typename
    that has NO wrapping Bramble.Node in the space (an
    unpromoted orphan)
  when: I type `@` and type a substring of `Y`'s display label
  then:
    - `Y` is NOT listed in the @-mention picker — orphan
      payloads are reached via the per-typename supertag-node
      landing page, not via @-mention;
    - if `Y` is the only matching candidate, the picker shows
      no matches; otherwise the picker shows only Bramble.Node
      entries whose resolved display labels also match the
      substring.
```

