      R-Bramble-Subject-Path, which the resolver maps to the
      Node representing today's date (the Node carrying the
      `#Day` supertag whose date is today's local-tz
      `YYYY-MM-DD`);
    - if no such Node existed yet, one is created (along
      with the `#Day` instance for today).
```

```mdl
test T-Today-Resets-Zoom: activating Today from any non-today subject navigates back to today's day-Node, regardless of prior zoom state
  given: a space whose Bramble exists with today's day-Node
    `D` and a Bramble.Node `X` reachable in the space
    (e.g. a descendant of `D`, a supertag-node, an
    `@`-mention destination, or any other Bramble.Node)
  and: the active pane's subject is `X`'s canonical path —
    i.e. the pane is on any Node other than today's day-Node
    via the Today alias
  when: the user activates the "Today" item in the sidebar's
    "Bramble" section
  then:
    - the pane's subject becomes the Today alias via
      `LayoutOperation.Open` per
      `F-Bramble-Nav.today-resets-zoom` +
      R-Bramble-Subject-Path — independent of what `X` was;
    - the Article re-renders with today's day-Node `D` as
      its pageNode per F-Zoom.subject-change-replaces-
      rendered-target;
    - any prior zoom state for `X` is naturally absent in the
      new render — the pane shows `D`'s full view as if
      newly opened.
```

```mdl
test T-Zoom-Writes-Subject-Path: clicking a bullet's marker changes the pane subject to that Node's canonical path
  given: a pane displays Bramble.Node `R` as its current
    subject; `R` has a structural child `X` rendered as a
    bullet in the pane
  when: the user clicks `X`'s bullet (no modifier)
  then:
    - the pane's subject becomes `X`'s canonical path via
      `LayoutOperation.Open` per F-Zoom.click-changes-subject
      + R-Bramble-Subject-Path;
    - the Article re-renders with `X` as its pageNode — the
      pane's H1 shows `X`'s content and `X`'s structural
      children render below;
    - the predecessor breadcrumb shows `R` (and any other
      incoming-edge sources of `X`) per
      F-DAG.Phase3e.predecessor-nav.
```

```mdl
test T-Bramble-Nav-all-tags-opens-schema-node: All Tags item navigates to the per-space Schema Node
  given: a space whose Bramble exists
  when: the user activates the "All Tags" item in the
    sidebar's "Bramble" section
  then:
    - the active pane navigates to the per-space Schema
      Node — the Node under which every supertag class is
      materialised per F-Supertag.eager-materialization.
```

```mdl
test T-Bramble-Nav-section-expands-on-bramble-creation: section is open on first appearance
  given: a space with no Bramble; the Bramble plugin is
    enabled; the user has the space create-menu open
  when: the user selects "Bramble" and the navigator
    re-renders with the new section present
  then:
    - the new "Bramble" section is visible AND its chevron
      is in the open state — Today and All Tags are visible
      without a click.
```

```mdl
test T-No-Root-graph-has-no-root-field: a Bramble.Graph carries no root reference
  given: a Bramble.Graph exists in any space
  when: an observer inspects the Graph's fields
  then:
    - the Graph carries no field designating a root Node;
    - the Graph's observable fields are metadata only
      (today: `name`).
```

```mdl
test T-No-Root-graph-not-directly-viewable: opening the Bramble.Graph itself renders nothing
  given: a Bramble exists in the space
  when: the active pane is navigated to the Bramble.Graph
    object (via a deep-link URL or programmatic open)
  then:
    - no article surface renders the Bramble.Graph as its
      subject — the user does not see "the Bramble" as a
      viewable object;
    - the practical entry points to the Bramble's content
      are its Nodes (Today, All Tags, …) per F-Bramble-Nav.
```

```mdl
test T-No-Root-create-navigates-to-today: creating a Bramble lands the user on today's Node
  given: a space with no Bramble; the user invokes the space
    create-menu's "Bramble" item
  when: the create-menu action completes
  then:
    - the active pane is navigated to today's Node (the Node
      carrying the `#Day` supertag for today's local-tz
      date — find-or-created as needed);
    - NOT to the Bramble.Graph object;
    - the navigator's "Bramble" section appears per
      F-Bramble-Nav.section-present-iff-bramble-exists.
```

```mdl
test T-No-Root-create-focuses-pane-cursor: after creation the pane cursor is ready to type
  given: a space with no Bramble; the Bramble plugin is
    enabled; the user has the space create-menu open
  when: the user selects "Bramble"
  then:
    - after the create-flow completes, the cursor is in the
      pane's focused Node's editor — typing a key delivers
      the keystroke without a separate click.
```

```mdl
test T-Versioning-pin-on-edge-create: creating a `'is-run-of'` edge captures the target's heads
  given: a Step Node S exists in the space; a Run Node R is
    being created (e.g. via F-New-Run-On-Step)
  when: `createEdge(db, R, S, { kind: 'is-run-of' })` runs
  then:
    - the resulting Edge carries a `targetVersion` field
      whose value equals `Obj.encodeVersion(Obj.version(S))`
      at the moment of edge creation;
    - call sites did not pass a separate "pin" argument —
      the `kind: 'is-run-of'` membership in
      `PINNING_EDGE_KINDS` was the sole trigger.
```

```mdl
test T-Versioning-pinned-edge-renders-snapshot: a pinned edge resolves to the target at the pinned version
  given: a Run R is `'is-run-of'` Step S, where the edge's
    `targetVersion` was captured when S.content was
    "Reconcile EOB"
  when: the user opens R as the page node and
    F-Run-Execution-View calls `resolveEdgeTarget` on the
    `'is-run-of'` edge
  then:
    - the resolved target's `content` reads "Reconcile EOB"
      (the pinned snapshot), regardless of any later edits
      to the live S;
    - the live S in the navigator still shows whatever its
      latest content is (the pin doesn't shadow live-S
      navigation).
```

```mdl
test T-Versioning-live-target-edits-do-not-disturb-pinned-view: edits to the live target are invisible to pinned views
  given: a Run R is `'is-run-of'` Step S, where the pinned
    snapshot reads "Reconcile EOB"; R is open as the page
    node
  when: the user opens S in a second pane and edits S's
    content to "Reconcile EOB (revised)"
  then:
    - S's chip in the navigator reflects the rename live;
    - R's Run Execution View continues to render
      "Reconcile EOB" (the pinned snapshot) — no
      retroactive change;
    - re-mounting R produces the same pinned-snapshot
      render.
```

```mdl
test T-Versioning-unpinned-edges-render-live: pre-versioning edges render live (greenfield)
  given: a Run R is `'is-run-of'` Step S via an edge whose
    `targetVersion` is unset (the edge predates
    F-Versioning, or its kind is not in `PINNING_EDGE_KINDS`)
  when: `resolveEdgeTarget` is called
  then:
    - the LIVE S is returned;
    - subsequent edits to S propagate into R's render per
      F-4b live-rename semantics — same behavior as before
      F-Versioning shipped.
```

```mdl
test T-Versioning-pin-survives-target-deletion: pinned edges keep rendering after the live target is marked deleted
  given: a Run R `'is-run-of'` Step S with the edge pinned
    at S's then-current heads; S is subsequently marked
    deleted (`db.remove`, retirement, etc. — non-destructive
    per substrate-principles §10)
  when: the user opens R and `resolveEdgeTarget` runs on the
    pinned edge
  then:
    - the pinned snapshot of S still renders (the snapshot
      reads from S's Automerge history, which persists
      regardless of the live `ObjectDeletedId` mark);
    - if `checkoutVersion` itself fails on S (privacy-
      deletion out of v1 scope), the resolver returns a
      sentinel and the renderer surfaces a `[removed]`
      placeholder — no crash.
```

